WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.440
The projection theorem, Theorem 4.2.7.

2
00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:06.443
If q one through q m is an orthonormal basis of a subspace U,

3
00:00:06.443 --> 00:00:10.851
then the projection of x onto U is the sum of the terms

4
00:00:10.851 --> 00:00:13.225
x dot q i, times q i.

5
00:00:13.625 --> 00:00:14.655
Take Example 4.2.11.

6
00:00:14.655 --> 00:00:20.410
U is the span of f one and f two, and x is two, zero, one.

7
00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:24.175
f one and f two are orthogonal, each with length root two,

8
00:00:24.175 --> 00:00:28.725
so normalize them to get an orthonormal basis, q one and q two.

9
00:00:29.125 --> 00:00:32.030
Project x onto the line spanned by q one.

10
00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:34.665
The coefficient x dot q one is root two,

11
00:00:34.665 --> 00:00:39.100
so this piece is root two times q one: one, one, zero.

12
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.990
Likewise, x dot q two is root two,

13
00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:44.225
giving one, negative one, zero.

14
00:00:44.625 --> 00:00:46.210
Now add the pieces.

15
00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.580
The projection of x onto U is two, zero, zero.

16
00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:52.579
The residual v, x minus p, is zero, zero, one.

17
00:00:52.579 --> 00:00:57.550
It is orthogonal to q one and q two, so it lies in U perp.

18
00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.565
So: find an orthonormal basis of U,

19
00:01:00.565 --> 00:01:03.775
project x onto each basis vector, and add.
